---
description: Run local tests after code changes and report results
alwaysApply: false
globs:
  - src/engine/**/*.js
  - src/state/**/*.js
  - src/data/**/*.js
  - src/ui/**/*.js
  - main.js
---

# Local test execution rule

When code changes touch the files matched above:

1. Run relevant local test commands before final response.
2. Prefer scoped runs first (`npm run test:unit` / `npm run test:integration`) and run full `npm test` when changes are broad.
3. If data definitions change (`src/data/**`), include `npm run test:data`.
4. If core flow/state changes (`src/engine/**`, `src/state/**`), include `npm run test:monte-carlo`.
5. Report to the user:
   - commands executed
   - pass/fail summary
   - blocking failures and the minimal next fix
6. If game progression flow changes (e.g. building unlock order, scheduled event timing, month pacing),
   update `docs/gameplay-flow-4-months.md` in the same change.

Do not claim tests passed unless commands were actually executed.
